<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anatoly Stessel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1915</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Anatoly Stoessel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anatoly Stessel was a Russian general who commanded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-arthur-tasmania">Port Arthur</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a>. After a siege of more than five months he surrendered the fortress to the Japanese in January 1905, while it still had men and supplies. A Russian court-martial sentenced him to death, commuted to imprisonment, and he was pardoned in 1909.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anatoly-stessel.jpg" alt="Anatoly Stessel" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatoly-stessel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
